<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Commune of Pavia</h1><p class="st-meta">1100 CE – 1359 CE (approx.) · capital Pavia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The old Lombard royal capital turned city-republic, a loyal imperial ally and Milan's bitter rival until the Visconti took it in 1359.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Pavia had been the capital of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Kingdom of the Lombards</a> and the coronation city of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-italy-medieval">Kingdom of Italy (medieval)</a>. Around 1100 its citizens organised a commune under consuls, inheriting the city's royal palace traditions and a renowned school of law.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consuls</a> and later a podestà ruled the city, which stood firmly with the emperors against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a>, fighting it repeatedly in the 12th and 13th centuries. Pavia controlled the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ticino-river">Ticino</a> and the Po and much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lomellina">Lomellina</a>. Its churches, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-michele-maggiore-pavia">San Michele Maggiore</a> where kings were crowned and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-pietro-in-ciel-doro">San Pietro in Ciel d'Oro</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augustine-of-hippo">Saint Augustine's</a> tomb, reflected its royal past. The Beccaria family dominated in the 14th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galeazzo-ii-visconti">Galeazzo II Visconti</a> captured Pavia in 1359 after a long siege, absorbing it into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-milan">Lordship of Milan</a>. The Visconti built a castle there, founded the university in 1361 and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/certosa-di-pavia">Certosa di Pavia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1100 CE – 1359 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V